  "answer": "Based on the ABS Census QuickStats data for 2016 and 2021, here are the calculations for the proportion of median weekly rent to median weekly household income for each state:\n\n**2016 proportions:**\n- NSW: $380 / $1,486 = **25.57%**\n- Victoria: $325 / $1,419 = **22.90%**\n- Queensland: $330 / $1,402 = **23.54%**\n\n**2021 proportions:**\n- NSW: $420 / $1,829 = **22.96%**\n- Victoria: $370 / $1,759 = **21.03%**\n- Queensland: $365 / $1,675 = **21.79%**\n\n**Decrease from 2016 to 2021 (percentage points):**\n- NSW: 25.57% − 22.96% = **2.61 pp**\n- Victoria: 22.90% − 21.03% = **1.87 pp**\n- Queensland: 23.54% − 21.79% = **1.75 pp**\n\n**Queensland** had the smallest decrease in the proportion of median weekly rent to median weekly household income from 2016 to 2021, at **1.75 percentage points**.",
